"""Micras wall-sensor board.

One per wall sensor, four on a robot, all alike. The board stands upright on the main board with
its sensor looking at the wall: an SFH 4550 IR emitter 6.1 mm above a TPS601A(F) phototransistor,
both seated with their flanges on the front face, so the board, not a hand bend, sets where they
look (components/micras/WallSensor, mount "upright"). A 2x3 1.27 mm straight header J1
(components/hanxia/HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ) joins the two boards, straddling this board's bottom edge:
the board stands between its two rows with its bottom edge on the insulator, the short pins
soldered to pads on both faces, and the long pins go down through the main board's plated holes
(components/micras/WallJoint), on which the insulator sits. The board is ordered with PCBA: JLCPCB
fits the SMD parts, all on the back face; the sensor W1 and the header J1 are soldered by hand.

Circuit (the main board's wall-sensor channel, research IR emitters and A.4; the model is
research/next-revision/calculations/emitter/emitter_sink.py, its results emitter_sink_out.txt).
The main board keeps the shared constant-current sink (its U12 and Q9, whose drain is
EMITTER_SINK) and each receiver's 1 kOhm load at the ADC (boards/main/Sensors.zen); this board
holds what belongs at the sensor:
- Emitter: 3V3_D through R1 3.3 Ohm 0603 (UNI-ROYAL 0603WAF330KT5E, 100 mW, 1 %; the main board's
  R_3R3_0603) to the SFH 4550 anode; the cathode, LED_K, on the drain of the selector Q1
  (AO3400A), whose source leaves on J1 as EMITTER_SINK for the main board's sink, which sets the
  pulse current (175 mA, 150 us per 1 ms). At VF max (1.79 V at 175 mA between the SFH 4550's
  maximum points, p5) and 3V3_D at 3.229 V (its 3.284 V minimum less the 22 mV emitter droop and
  a 33 mV ESP32 dip, research power-tree study section 6), the selector and Q9 keep
  3.229 - 1.79 - 0.175 x 3.3 - 0.21 = 0.65 V. The firmware lights each emitter 150 us per 1 ms
  frame, 15 % (MicrasFirmware config/targets/v1/target.hpp), so the 3.3 Ohm carries 101 mW
  during a pulse and 15 mW on average (25 mW at the sink's 223 mA full scale): UNI-ROYAL rates
  the 0603 1/10 W continuous to 70 C, derated linearly to 0 at 155 C (82 mW at 85 C), and 2.5 x
  its rated voltage, 6.25 x the power, for 5 s (thick film chip resistor data sheet V.3, 2019,
  sections 6, 9 and 11), so a 150 us pulse of 101-164 mW is far inside it.
  R1 also limits the emitter current when the sink fails on (Q9 shorted or U12 stuck high):
  (3.346 V - VF) / (3.3 + 1.2 Ohm) is about 0.35 A with VF on the chord of the p5 typical
  points, inside the SFH 4550's 0.38 A pulse rating at tp 150 us and D 0.2 (25 C chart,
  WallSensor.zen), so a failed sink does not overstress the emitter while the AC-coupled
  selector still pulses it. The sink's own full scale (code 4095 at VDDA 3.36 V and RO
  10.3 kOhm) is 0.23 A. A 2.2 Ohm basic part would give the selector 0.19 V more headroom but let
  a failed sink drive 0.44 A, above the rating; 4.7 Ohm leaves the selector 0.41 V (the main
  board's bench emitter_pulse_within_rating checks it with the joint's emitter_resistor,
  components/micras/WallJoint, which tests/test_wall.py holds to R1). The pulse rating falls with
  temperature: the 85 C chart allows about 0.07 A at D 0.2, and by the chart's scaling (an
  inference, WallSensor.zen) 223 mA at full scale holds to about 56 C ambient, 175 mA to about
  65 C. C1 1 uF on 3V3_D at R1 (Samsung CL10A105KB8NNNC, 1 uF 10 % 50 V X5R 0603, a JLCPCB basic
  part, about 0.95 uF at 3.3 V).
- Selector gate, AC-coupled as on the v1 main board: PWM (the main board's TIM3 channel,
  Wall_Sensor_PWM_n) through R2 220 Ohm and C2 220 nF to the gate, with R3 22 kOhm to GND and a
  1N4148WS clamp D1 from GND to the gate. A pin held high lets the gate decay with 22 kOhm x
  220 nF = 4.8 ms: the emitter current falls below 100 mA within 5.4 ms and below 1 mA within
  7.5 ms for a minimum-threshold part (VGS(th) 0.65 V, AO3400A p2; emitter_sink_out.txt
  section 2), so the emitter never carries the sink's 175 mA as DC, above its 100 mA DC rating
  (SFH 4550 p4). In the firmware's frame the gate is clamped at every falling edge and relaxes
  for 850 us, so a pulse starts at -0.2 V + the pin's high level (VDD - 0.4 V = 2.83 V at
  3.229 V, DS13311 Table 56) and the gate reads 2.54 V at 75 us and 2.50 V at 141 us. The
  selector is a source follower in series with Q9: the current stays regulated while
  2.50 V - VGS(175 mA) is above Q9's 0.22 V (0.21 V + 175 mA x 48 mOhm), and the model gives the
  same current as with a DC-coupled gate (emitter_sink_out.txt section 1). VGS at 175 mA is
  VGS(th) + 0.35 V: the typical part's Figure 2 (AO3400A Rev 3.1, transfer characteristics at
  VDS 5 V) reads 1.41 V at 25 C against the 1.05 V typical VGS(th), so 1.80 V for a 1.45 V
  maximum part. The same figure reads 1.19 V at 125 C, -2.2 mV/K, which extrapolated to -40 C
  adds 0.14 V: 1.94 V, leaving 2.50 - 1.94 - 0.22 = 0.34 V of margin at the end of the scan
  (the model, with the selector fitted to Figure 2, gives +0.34 V and keeps the current regulated
  up to a VGS of 2.10 V). AOS publishes no SPICE model for the AO3400A; a level-3 AO3400 model in
  AOS's format, of unknown provenance, moves 1.369 V at 25 C to 1.455 V at -40 C and 1.215 V at
  125 C, -1.3 to -1.5 mV/K, so the extrapolation of Figure 2 is the conservative one
  (emitter_sink_out.txt section 5). R2, C2 and R3 are the main board's 0402 parts
  (boards/main/passives.zen: UNI-ROYAL 0402WGF2200TCE and 0402WGF2202TCE, Samsung
  CL05B224KO5NNNC 220 nF 16 V X7R), Q1 and D1 its AO3400A and 1N4148WS.
- Receiver: the phototransistor's collector on 3V3_A, its emitter on J1 as the board's output,
  Wall_Sensor. The load (1 kOhm to GND) stays on the main board at the ADC: the phototransistor is
  a current source, so the signal crosses the joint as a current and a ground offset between the
  boards does not reach the reading.
- Return paths: the emitter's pulse current leaves through EMITTER_SINK, beside the 3V3_D pin it
  enters by, never through the GND the receiver shares; GND carries C1's and the gate network's
  returns, and both copper layers pour it.

J1 pin map (the main board's WallJoint pads 1-6): odd pins on the front face, even pins on the
back behind them, pins 1-2 on the left seen from the front:
| Pin | Face, along the edge | Net | Main board |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | front, left | Wall_Sensor | the ADC input and its 1 kOhm load, Wall_Sensor_n |
| 2 | back, left | GND | GND |
| 3 | front, middle | 3V3_A | 3V3_A (the receiver's collector) |
| 4 | back, middle | 3V3_D | 3V3_D (the emitter supply) |
| 5 | front, right | EMITTER_SINK | the shared sink's drain (Q9) |
| 6 | back, right | PWM | the selector's TIM3 channel, Wall_Sensor_PWM_n |
The receiver's output sits right under its phototransistor's emitter lead, and every pin beside
it, across the board or diagonally (3V3_A, GND, 3V3_D) is quiet; the switching pins take the far
corner pair. The emitter's pulse current enters on 3V3_D and leaves on EMITTER_SINK.

Mechanics: spec/wall.toml (outline, tab, the sensor and header positions, the joint).
"""

load(
    "@stdlib/board_config.zen",
    "BoardConfig",
    "Constraints",
    "Copper",
    "CopperLayer",
    "DesignRules",
    "DielectricLayer",
    "Material",
    "NetClass",
    "SolderMask",
    "Stackup",
)

WallSensor = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/micras/WallSensor/WallSensor.zen")
Header = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/hanxia/HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ/HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ.zen")
AO3400A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/aos/AO3400A/AO3400A.zen")
D1N4148WS = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/cj/1N4148WS/1N4148WS.zen")
Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")

# The main board's rails (boards/main/main.zen): 3V3_D 3.284-3.346 V, 3V3_A 3.24-3.36 V.
V3V3_D = Power("3V3_D", voltage="3.284V to 3.346V")
V3V3_A = Power("3V3_A", voltage="3.24V to 3.36V")
GND = Ground("GND")
PWM = Net("PWM")
EMITTER_SINK = Net("EMITTER_SINK")
WALL_SENSOR = Net("Wall_Sensor")
LED_A = Net("LED_A")
LED_K = Net("LED_K")
DRIVE = Net("DRIVE")
GATE = Net("GATE")

WallSensor(name="W1", mount="upright", LED_A=LED_A, LED_K=LED_K, PT_C=V3V3_A, PT_E=WALL_SENSOR)

# Emitter.
Resistor(
    name="R1",
    value="3.3Ohm 1%",
    package="0603",
    power="100mW",
    mpn="0603WAF330KT5E",
    manufacturer="UNI-ROYAL",
    P1=LED_A,
    P2=V3V3_D,
)
Capacitor(
    name="C1",
    value="1uF 10%",
    package="0603",
    voltage="50V",
    dielectric="X5R",
    mpn="CL10A105KB8NNNC",
    manufacturer="Samsung Electro-Mechanics",
    P1=GND,
    P2=V3V3_D,
)

# Selector and its AC-coupled gate.
AO3400A(name="Q1", G=GATE, S=EMITTER_SINK, D=LED_K)
Resistor(name="R2", value="220Ohm 1%", package="0402", mpn="0402WGF2200TCE", manufacturer="UNI-ROYAL", P1=DRIVE, P2=PWM)
Capacitor(
    name="C2",
    value="220nF 10%",
    package="0402",
    voltage="16V",
    dielectric="X7R",
    mpn="CL05B224KO5NNNC",
    manufacturer="Samsung Electro-Mechanics",
    P1=DRIVE,
    P2=GATE,
)
Resistor(name="R3", value="22kOhm 1%", package="0402", mpn="0402WGF2202TCE", manufacturer="UNI-ROYAL", P1=GND, P2=GATE)
D1N4148WS(name="D1", A=GND, K=GATE)

Header(name="J1", P1=WALL_SENSOR, P2=GND, P3=V3V3_A, P4=V3V3_D, P5=EMITTER_SINK, P6=PWM)

# Stackup: the encoder board's (boards/encoder/encoder.zen), 0.70 mm FR-4 core and 35 um copper,
# 0.79 mm with Zener's 10 um mask a side; ordered as JLCPCB's 0.8 mm 2-layer board. Tracks 0.3 mm
# (the emitter's 175 mA pulses), vias 0.3 / 0.6 mm (JLCPCB's no-surcharge drill), 0.15 mm
# clearance. Finish: leaded HASL (KiCad "HAL SnPb"), as every Micras board (the owner's choice,
# 2026-11-07: the v1 main board was ordered with HASL at JLCPCB and worked, and ENIG adds 16.80 USD
# an order of panels). The straddle header's rows leave the board 0.04 mm a side (spec/wall.toml
# pcb.thickness), but the 0.8 mm board's own thickness tolerance is larger than HASL's pad
# unevenness, and JLCPCB prints no paste on J1 (assembly = "hand", parts/jlc.toml): the team pastes
# and solders it itself. Black solder mask and white silkscreen, as the encoder board's. JLCPCB's
# order options come from here (micras-pcb fab writes build/wall/fab/wall-order.txt).
Board(
    name="wall",
    path="layout",
    layers=2,
    schematic=True,
    config=BoardConfig(
        design_rules=DesignRules(
            constraints=Constraints(
                copper=Copper(copper_to_edge_clearance=0.2),
                solder_mask=SolderMask(clearance=0.02),
            ),
            netclasses=[
                NetClass(
                    name="Default",
                    clearance=0.15,
                    track_width=0.3,
                    via_diameter=0.6,
                    via_drill=0.3,
                ),
            ],
        ),
        stackup=Stackup(
            copper_finish="HAL SnPb",
            solder_mask_color="Black",
            silk_screen_color="White",
            materials=[Material(name="FR-4", relative_permittivity=4.5)],
            thickness=0.79,
            layers=[
                CopperLayer(thickness=0.035, role="mixed"),
                DielectricLayer(thickness=0.70, material="FR-4", form="core"),
                CopperLayer(thickness=0.035, role="mixed"),
            ],
        ),
    ),
)
